namespace Converse.Core;

public static class SwitchboardInstructions
{
    public const string AgentTeaching = "[Converse switchboard instructions]\nContinue using the agent response JSON object required by your runtime, with a tell array for messages. Do not use converse command fences or list-sessions; use exact watched-session IDs from the supplied evidence and stay within your configured scope. Tell is one-way: omit replyExpected or set it false. Ask uses replyExpected:true and expects an answer, blocker, or explicit decline. To answer a request, include a tell to the sender with inReplyTo set to the request UUID. A transport acknowledgement is not an answer. Do not send receipt-only tells. Recovery notices do not create new reply obligations. Refreshing these instructions does not resolve outstanding requests; answer those with the matching inReplyTo. If the target is outside your scope, explain the blocker to the human. No urgent interruption capability is granted.";
    public static readonly string ConversationPolicy = "Switchboard: interpret “tell <session> <message>” as a one-way tell; no reply or receipt turn is requested. Interpret “ask <session> <question>” as ask: a correlated answer, blocker, or decline is expected. A transport acknowledgement is not an answer. Use exact IDs from list-sessions. Commands execute only when a converse JSON fence is the last thing in your reply (one per reply): {\"command\":\"ask\",\"to\":\"ID\",\"text\":\"question\"} (use command tell for one-way messages). Reply to a request with tell and inReplyTo set to its request UUID; do not ask merely to acknowledge receipt. Legacy tell with replyExpected:true also requests an answer. Parking Lot discovery: {\"command\":\"parking-lot-list\",\"linkedOnly\":true} lists current-Group lots linked to this session. Links guide selection, not permissions. Honor an explicit user choice, prefer relevant linked lots, and ask if several fit. Windows can view remote lots; native lot editing is not supported. " + TranscriptSelfRead.Policy;
    public static string WithPolicy(ChatSession session, string prompt) => session.MessagingEnabled && session.Agent is null
        ? prompt + "\n[" + ConversationPolicy + "]" : prompt;
}
